From: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
Date: Fri, 09 Oct 2026 14:09:12 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: mt7915: reject a background CAC on a non-radar channel

A background CAC request whose control channel has no radar flag
takes the stop path. The driver stops the background chain, records
the chandef and returns success, but no radar detector runs. cfg80211
then times the CAC and at the end marks the radar channels of the
block as available. With a chain already on a radar channel, the same
request starts a detector on the block instead.

Return -EINVAL for such a chandef before any firmware command, also
when a chain runs. The driver then keeps its record of the chain, and
the caller sees the refusal.

Fixes: 78770f741af9 ("mt76: mt7915: introduce mt7915_set_radar_background routine")
Signed-off-by: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
---
 mt7915/main.c |    6 ++++--
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

--- a/mt7915/main.c
+++ b/mt7915/main.c
@@ -1794,13 +1794,15 @@ mt7915_set_radar_background(struct ieee8
 		goto out;
 	}
 
+	if (chandef && !(chandef->chan->flags & IEEE80211_CHAN_RADAR))
+		goto out;
+
 	/* rdd2 already configured on a radar channel */
 	running = dev->rdd2_phy &&
 		  cfg80211_chandef_valid(&dev->rdd2_chandef) &&
 		  !!(dev->rdd2_chandef.chan->flags & IEEE80211_CHAN_RADAR);
 
-	if (!chandef || running ||
-	    !(chandef->chan->flags & IEEE80211_CHAN_RADAR)) {
+	if (!chandef || running) {
 		ret = mt7915_mcu_rdd_background_enable(phy, NULL);
 		if (ret)
 			goto out;
